A||N||9||BlackARROW||Interior light won't turn off||||1||
Z||000000||BlackARROW||09-28-2001||07:59 PM||||Weird<BR>I came home, open my door, was putting some Simoniz stuff, making my interior shine a bit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, not putting anything anywhere a wire or a switch, than I shut the door, and the light won't come off.  I took the door switch, trying to test it - no power on both wire. I removed the Top Panel (with courtesy light) to see if there was no problem with the center switch, but even disconnecting the set - my floor light was still on. Well well.. Then it's making ground somewhere.  No? But where?  <P>Any of you know the electrical part a bit?  In my Haynes book, looking at the diagram, I think I should follow the white wire for a ground problem - but another thing that's weird; I had to pull out 1 fuse for the courtesy light, and another fuse for the floor lights. On the diagram, it indicates only 1 fuse for it. <P>Any idea where that white wire start, and ends - and go by maybe?<P>Thanks a lot.. <P><P>------------------<BR>BlackARROW &gt;&gt;--&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85<BR>"Get your groove on"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||09-28-2001||08:06 PM||||The lights come on whenever one of the door switches go to ground, ergo you've got a grounded wire/switch somewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||09-28-2001||08:25 PM||||Have you checked the panel dimmer switch?<BR>Sounds like in your wiping you have turned it on inadvertently!||||reg||1
